    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nae_121'), 'The hint service before the fix:

const prompt = HINT_TEMPLATE
  .replaceAll("{{learnerCode}}", dto.code)
  .replaceAll("{{challengeTitle}}", challenge.title);

The learner''s code, sent with the hint request:

// TODO: print {{challengeTitle}} in the header
console.log(sum([1, 2, 3]));

challenge.title is "Sum of an array".

Statement: "The rendered prompt contains the learner''s code exactly as the learner typed it."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The first replaceAll puts the learner''s code into the template. The second replaceAll then scans the whole string again, the inserted code included, so the comment becomes "// TODO: print Sum of an array in the header". The model now reads code the learner never wrote. A renderer must read the template once and insert each value without scanning it again, because learner code is untrusted input and can contain anything, template syntax included. (A string passed as the replacement to replace or replaceAll has a second trap: "$&" and "$''" in it are replacement patterns.) The misconception is that replacing variables one after another is the same as rendering once. It is the same only while no value contains placeholder syntax, and you do not control the values.', 1, 5
