WITH q AS (
    INSERT INTO challenge.questions (challenge_id, question, type, explanation, order_index, points)
    SELECT (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nae_211'), 'callModel() in the hint service:
async function callModel(messages: Message[]): Promise<Reply> {
  for (let attempt = 1; attempt <= 3; attempt++) {
    try {
      return await llm.complete(messages);
    } catch (err) {
      if (attempt === 3) throw err;
      await sleep(500 * 2 ** (attempt - 1));
    }
  }
  throw new Error("unreachable");
}

Log after the provider key was rotated on Friday (the new key had not reached the hint service yet):
18:02:11.000 hint req=h_9a01 call=1 status=401 error=invalid_api_key
18:02:11.512 hint req=h_9a01 call=2 status=401 error=invalid_api_key
18:02:12.519 hint req=h_9a01 call=3 status=401 error=invalid_api_key
18:02:12.523 hint req=h_9a01 -> 500 Internal Server Error

Statement: "Because the loop is bounded to 3 attempts and backs off, retrying the 401 is a reasonable choice: the key may become valid on a later attempt."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A 401 says the credentials are wrong; the same request with the same key gets the same answer half a second later, so every hint request now costs three calls and 1.5 s of waiting before the learner sees a 500. A limit and backoff make a retry cheaper, not useful. Classify first: retry only transient failures (429, 502, 503, 504, timeouts), and for 400/401/403 return the fallback hint at once and raise an alert, because a human has to fix the key. The misconception is that a bounded retry is harmless for any error.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nae_211') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
)
