VALUES ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_nae_212'), 1, 'Three different things can happen on each call: it throws a transient error, it throws a permanent error, or it returns text that may or may not pass validateHint. Which counter does each case use up, and which messages does the next call send?'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_nae_212'), 2, 'Look at what you pass to llm.complete after an invalid reply: repairMessages(reply.text, errors) replaces the messages, it is not appended to them. Then look at where you increase calls: before the try, so a call that throws is counted too.'),
       ((SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_coding_nae_212'), 3, 'A similar loop on other data: an image service that retries ''busy'' with waits of 200 and 400 ms, and on a ''blurry'' result sends one ''sharpen'' request with only that image, then gives up with a placeholder. One loop, two counters (retries, sharpen requests), each checked before it is used, and the placeholder returned from every exit that is not a success.');
