Statement: "Retrying call 1 was free: we aborted it after 10 s, so the provider never finished it and did not count its tokens."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The export shows the first request (started at 10:03:07, the moment call 1 was sent) completed on the provider''s side with 380 output tokens, after we had stopped waiting. Aborting stops our client from waiting; it does not reliably stop the work already sent, and the provider''s usage, and possibly the bill, can include it. Check your provider''s documentation for how cancelled requests are counted. So a retry after a timeout is not free and not idempotent in cost: keep timeouts above the normal slow case, bound the retries, and give each hint request an idempotency key so a double click or a client retry reuses one result instead of calling the model again.', 3, 5
