const key = `hint:${req.challengeSlug}:${sha256(req.learnerCode + "\n" + req.failingTest)}`;
const cached = await cache.get(key);
if (cached) return cached;
const hint = await createHint(req);   // renders the current prompt version
await cache.set(key, hint, { ttlSeconds: 86_400 });

Deploy log:
2026-10-20 10:00  hint prompt hint-v4 -> hint-v5 (shorter hints, no code blocks)

Support ticket, 2026-10-20 15:30: "I still get the long hints with code blocks on Top words."

Statement: "Learners whose code and failing test were already in the cache keep getting hints written with hint-v4 until those entries expire, up to 24 hours after they were stored."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. The key is built from the challenge, the learner''s code and the failing test only. Nothing in it changes when the prompt goes from v4 to v5, so a request that matches an entry stored before the deploy reads the v4 hint, and only requests with new code reach hint-v5. The entries leave the cache when their 24-hour TTL ends. The fix is to put everything that changes the answer into the key: the prompt version, the model and its parameters, and the reference version of the challenge. Then a deploy makes the old entries unreachable at once, with no mass delete. The misconception is that deploying a new prompt changes every answer immediately; a response cache keeps serving what the old prompt wrote.', 1, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_nae_421') AND order_index = 1)
    RETURNING id
)
